From b270a7bd73bac5eb5b3e4a62c67f9a6125bbc0aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:53:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(process): a gateway restart re-attaches sandbox
 background jobs or tells the session its watcher is lost [daveey]

Recovery skipped every pid_scope=sandbox checkpoint entry ("in-sandbox PIDs mean nothing once
the env handle is gone"), and only Desktop/TUI owners got the exited-while-unwatched wake. A
Slack session that ended its turn on "I'll report when it finishes" was never woken
(alpha-askeve 2026-10-30: qa.sh pid 7331 kept running in its persistent container and exited 0
at 10:50; nobody watched it).

- spawn_via_env records env.reattach_handle() (Docker: exe + container id) and the sandbox temp
  dir in processes.json.
- Recovery re-attaches when the container is still running and the job's wrapper files exist
  (tools/environments/reattach.py: docker exec only, never creates or restarts a container),
  restarts the poller and the gateway watcher, so the real exit code and output tail arrive.
- Otherwise the owning session gets a one-shot "watcher lost at restart, status unknown" notice:
  gateway sessions through a recovered watcher, Desktop chats through the re-adopt sink.
- Gateway-owned host jobs that exited while unwatched (or exit after re-adoption) now wake their
  session with the status-unknown completion instead of vanishing.
- One log line per re-attached or abandoned process, naming the session.
